SNK Neo Geo (MVS/AES) core: the chip models of MiSTer's NeoGeo core, GPL v2 or later (the Sean Gonsalves files), FX68K and jt10 / jt49 GPL v3,
T80 BSD-style.
Rights holders who see a problem with any part listed here: please contact us, and we remove the part concerned.

What is here. These files are the parts of https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/NeoGeo_MiSTer (commit ffaab14, 2026-09-01, "Update README.md") that the
core uses, copied unchanged by tools/vendor_neogeo.sh (SHA256SUMS lists them):
  neogeo.sv           the upstream top (the MiSTer "emu" module). Kept as the reference our cores/neogeo/trx/neo_core.v derives from; it is NOT built.
  cells/, io/, video/ the chip models of the MVS/AES board: NEO-C1, D0, E0, F0, G0, B1, ZMC, ZMC2, LSPC2-A2, the cartridge chips (NEO-PVC, NEO-SMA,
                      NEO-CMC), the system latch, the uPD4990 clock, the watchdog and the cell library. Sean 'Furrtek' Gonsalves, copyright 2018;
                      the headers say GNU GPL "version 2 of the License, or (at your option) any later version" (io, mem) and "version 3 ... or any
                      later version" (cells, most of video). register.v (four lines) has no header.
  cpu/                cpu_68k.v, cpu_z80.v (the wrappers, GPL v3 and v2 or later), FX68K (Jorge Cwik, copyright 2018; fx68k.txt carries the GPL
                      "version 3 ... or (at your option) any later version" text for the directory; fx68k.sv itself names the copyright only;
                      microrom.mem and nanorom.mem are the 68000 core's own microcode tables), T80 (Daniel Wallner, MikeJ, Sorgelig: BSD-style
                      redistribution conditions in the headers, kept).
  jt12/hdl, jt49/hdl the YM2610 (jt10) and YM2149 (jt49) cores of Jose Tejada, as jt10.qip / jt49.qip list them; GPL v3 (own LICENSE files,
                      headers "version 3 ... or any later version"). jt12_pcm.v has no header. The manuals of the upstream tree are not copied.
  LICENSE             the upstream repository's top-level licence text (GNU GPL version 2).

What is not here: sys/ (the MiSTer framework: HPS, scaler, OSD), pll/, the Neo Geo CD (rtl/cd: the CD controller, the drive model, CDDA and the
CEGen clock helper, spec T143 D4a), mem/ (dpram.v with altsyncram, ddram.sv, sdram.sv and sdram_mux.sv by Sorgelig, memcard.v and backup.v by Sean Gonsalves: replaced by cores/neogeo/trx/neo_ram.v, neo_mux.v, neo_mem.v, neo_memcard.v and neo_bk.v, which keep the interfaces),
the Quartus projects, releases/ (the upstream bitstreams), DEV_NOTES.md and xml.md (read for the file layout only, nothing copied), the romsets.xml
set lists. No ROM, BIOS, game or ROM-set file is here or ever goes into this repository, a bench, a package or a .cfw: the BIOS (sp-s2.sp1,
uni-bios.rom or neo-epo.sp1), 000-lo.lo and sfix.sfix, and the games are the user's own and arrive from the user's SD card or the core folder.

What is built from them is these files plus cores/neogeo/trx/neo_core.v, which is cores/neogeo/rtl/neogeo.sv with the MiSTer framework, the
Neo Geo CD, the SDRAM / DDR3 controllers and the altsyncram memories taken out and the DDR2 memory service and the TRX register block put in
(the changes are marked "TRX" there). rtl/ itself is never edited: tools/check_neogeo_tree.py keeps it on SHA256SUMS.

What the licence means here. GPL v3 or later covers the gateware of this core and everything linked into its bitstream (every group above is
"v3" or "v2 or later"; T80's BSD notice stays with it). A .cfw of this core that is given to a third party has to come with its corresponding
source: that is this directory (the upstream copy), cores/neogeo/trx and cores/neogeo/layer2_neogeo.v (our glue), cores/neogeo/mono (the build
recipe) and tools/vendor_neogeo.sh - all of it is in this repository. The host and the other cores are separate works and are not covered.
